    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **70 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` derived owner field so the application satisfies the specification.\n\n**Spec mapping** \u2014 `riskFlag` is `true` when any of three conditions hold, else `false`:\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2192 `owner.possibleDuplicate` is true (soft-match on soundex+postcode with a different telephone).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2192 any dot-separated label of the email domain matches a known disposable service name (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`). This deliberately catches variants that evade the exact blocklist rejected at creation \u2014 e.g. subdomains like `mail.mailinator.com` or alternate TLDs like `tempmail.net` \u2014 since the exact blocklisted domains never make it to a stored owner.\n3. **Over soft capacity** \u2192 `owner.capacityWarning` is true (city held 40\u201349 owners at creation, approaching the hard limit of 50).\n\n**Changes:**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` with the getter/setter).\n- `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `@Mapping` for `riskFlag`, plus `riskFlag(owner)` and `disposableAdjacentEmail(owner)` helper methods and the `DISPOSABLE_ADJACENT_LABELS` set, mirroring the existing derived-field style in this mapper.\n\nThe new `Cp58Tests` (riskFlag false for a normal owner) passes, as do the related duplicate/email tests (`Cp10`, `Cp35`, `Cp38`) and the entire 70-test suite.",
